# Implementation Plan: Port 05_agent_loop from Ruby to Python

## Goal Description
Port [`week1_baseline/ruby/05_agent_loop`](file:///Users/vivekmitra/Desktop/Learn2Code/Anthropic/claude-code-camp-2026-Q2/week1_baseline/ruby/05_agent_loop) to Python under [`week1_baseline/python/05_agent_loop`](file:///Users/vivekmitra/Desktop/Learn2Code/Anthropic/claude-code-camp-2026-Q2/week1_baseline/python/05_agent_loop).

The **Agent Loop** is the operational core of BOUKENSHA. Everything built prior—configuration, structs, registry, prompt builder, and HTTP client—provides the foundation. In Step 5, the `Agent` drives conversation turns in an iterative loop:
1. Formats messages and tools, and dispatches requests to the model.
2. Inspects normalized response stop reasons (`tool_use` vs `end_turn`).
3. Dispatches requested tool calls via `Registry`.
4. Injects tool results as `:tool_result` turns and continues to the next iteration.
5. Halts on `end_turn` and returns the final synthesized response.
6. Enforces iteration ceilings (`max_iterations`), executing a graceful wind-down call with tools disabled if the limit is reached.

Execution will use the shared root `.venv` via [`week1_baseline/bin/python/05_agent_loop.sh`](file:///Users/vivekmitra/Desktop/Learn2Code/Anthropic/claude-code-camp-2026-Q2/week1_baseline/bin/python/05_agent_loop.sh).

