## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Gemini Thought Signature Preservation**:
> Gemini 3 series models (e.g. `gemini-3.8-flash` configured in [`.boukensha/settings.yml`](file:///Users/vivekmitra/Desktop/Learn2Code/Anthropic/claude-code-camp-2026-Q2/.boukensha/settings.yml)) enforce thought signatures during multi-turn function calling. When Gemini generates a `functionCall`, it attaches a cryptographic `thoughtSignature` to that part. On subsequent turns when the conversation history is re-sent with the tool result, Gemini's API strictly requires that the historical `functionCall` part retain its `thoughtSignature`. Omitting it triggers a fatal HTTP 400 (`"Function call is missing a thought_signature in functionCall parts"`).
> 
> The Python port must preserve `thought_signature` / `thoughtSignature` in `Gemini.parse_response` and re-inject it on reconstructed model turn parts in `Gemini._assistant_parts`, matching our verified Ruby fix.

> [!NOTE]
> **Stateless Client and Tool Wind-Down**:
> `Client.call(builder, max_output_tokens=1024, tools=None)` accepts `tools`. In `Agent.run()`, default tools from the builder are used; during `Agent._wrap_up()`, `tools=[]` is explicitly passed to disable further tool calls while using the same stateless `Client` and `builder` instances.

