## Architecture Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant App as example.py
    participant Agent as Agent (Loop Orchestrator)
    participant Builder as PromptBuilder (Context + Backend)
    participant Client as Client (Stateless Transport)
    participant LLM as Provider API (Gemini / Anthropic / OpenAI / Ollama)
    participant Reg as Registry (Tool Dispatcher)

    App->>Agent: run()
    loop Until end_turn or max_iterations reached
        Agent->>Client: call(builder, max_output_tokens)
        Client->>Builder: url, headers, to_api_payload()
        Client->>LLM: HTTP POST (Payload with tools & history)
        LLM-->>Client: HTTP 200 (JSON Response)
        Client-->>Agent: Raw response dict
        Agent->>Builder: parse_response(response)
        Builder-->>Agent: Normalized {stop_reason, content: [...]}

        alt stop_reason == "tool_use"
            Agent->>Agent: Record assistant message with content blocks
            loop For each tool_use block
                Agent->>Reg: dispatch(name, input_args)
                Reg-->>Agent: Tool result string
                Agent->>Agent: Record tool_result message with tool_use_id
            end
            Note over Agent,Builder: Repeat loop with updated conversation history
        else stop_reason == "end_turn"
            Agent-->>App: Return final assistant text
        end
    end

    opt max_iterations reached
        Agent->>Agent: Record user wrap-up directive
        Agent->>Client: call(builder, tools=[], max_output_tokens=400)
        Client-->>Agent: Final summary response
        Agent-->>App: Return wind-down summary (or deterministic fallback)
    end
```

