#### [NEW] `week1_baseline/python/05_agent_loop/boukensha/agent.py`
The agent loop orchestrator:
- `MAX_ITERATIONS = 25`
- `WRAP_UP_OUTPUT_TOKENS = 400`
- `WRAP_UP_DIRECTIVE`: instructions requesting a concise wind-down summary without tool calls.
- `__init__(context, registry, builder, client, task_settings=None, max_iterations=None, max_output_tokens=None)`
- `run() -> str`: executes iterative turns until `end_turn` or `max_iterations`.
- `_handle_tool_calls(content)`: appends assistant turn to context, dispatches each tool, and appends `tool_result` turns.
- `_extract_text(content) -> str`: collects all text blocks.
- `_wrap_up(reason) -> str`: adds wrap-up directive and dispatches tools-disabled call via `client.call(self.builder, tools=[], max_output_tokens=WRAP_UP_OUTPUT_TOKENS)`.
- `_fallback_message(reason) -> str`: deterministic response if wind-down call fails.

